From: Guohan Lu <securely1g@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Derive multiarch include paths from declared Debian headers

Source: bazel-contrib/rules_distroless v0.9.4 (b9da1141985c4a84f696326006e0d85659c40747).
The pkg-config importer adds /usr/include/x86_64-linux-gnu on every CPU.
On ARM64, Lua 5.1 includes lua5.1-deb-multiarch.h from
/usr/include/aarch64-linux-gnu, so compiling the existing SONiC rsyslog
plugin tests fails even though the header is a declared package output.

Keep /usr/include and add only multiarch roots present in the package's
header inventory. This also handles armhf without guessing from repository
names or borrowing host headers. Production C++ sources remain unchanged.
The SONiC source owner tests AMD64, ARM64, armhf and ordinary header layouts;
the registry/consumer CI compiles a real Lua program on both native CPUs.

Related-Upstream: https://github.com/bazel-contrib/rules_distroless/pull/220
Related-Commit: 3b26479ff8eca6ac8b69c1a79ff47bc5a9d8bbc0 (Song Qing)
That closed, unmerged proposal also discovers multiarch roots from header paths.
This implementation targets the existing 0.9.4 importer rather than its API rewrite.
Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Guohan Lu <securely1g@gmail.com>
---
diff --git a/apt/private/deb_import.bzl b/apt/private/deb_import.bzl
--- a/apt/private/deb_import.bzl
+++ b/apt/private/deb_import.bzl
@@ -5,2 +5,3 @@
 load(":pkgconfig.bzl", "pkgconfig")
+load(":multiarch.bzl", "default_include_dirs")
 load(":util.bzl", "util")
@@ -374,3 +375,3 @@
                         "external/.." + include: True
-                        for include in includes + ["/usr/include", "/usr/include/x86_64-linux-gnu"]
+                        for include in includes + default_include_dirs(h_files + hpp_files + hpp_files_woext)
                     }.keys(),
diff --git a/apt/private/multiarch.bzl b/apt/private/multiarch.bzl
new file mode 100644
--- /dev/null
+++ b/apt/private/multiarch.bzl
@@ -0,0 +1,10 @@
+"""Default C/C++ include roots from the package's declared header inventory."""
+
+def default_include_dirs(headers):
+    """Include Debian multiarch roots only when this package declares headers there."""
+    includes = {"/usr/include": True}
+    for header in headers:
+        parts = header.split("/")
+        if len(parts) > 3 and parts[:2] == ["usr", "include"] and "-linux-" in parts[2]:
+            includes["/" + "/".join(parts[:3])] = True
+    return sorted(includes.keys())
